1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nxc6 bxc6 6. e5 Nd5 7. Bc4 Bb7 8. O-O Bc5 9. Nd2 Ne7 10. Ne4 Bb6 11. Qf3 O-O 12. Bd3 Kh8 13. Qh3 Ng6 14. Ng5 h6 15. Nf3 Re8 16. Bxh6 gxh6 17. Qxh6+ Kg8 18. Bxg6 fxg6 19. Qxg6+ Kh8 20. Ng5 Re7 21. Nf7+ Rxf7 22. Qxf7 Qe8 23. Qf6+ Kg8 24. Rad1 Rd8 25. Rd3 Qf8 26. Rg3+ Kh7 27. Rh3+ {Sources: The Field, 1 April 1911; Sunday Times, 2 April 1911} ({The shortest way would have been} 27. Qg6+ Kh8 28. Rh3+ {and mate next move. The game was prolonged to 40 moves, but the ending being of no interest it is omitted. (The Field)}) 27... Kg8 28. Qg5+ $2 (28. Rh8#) 28... Kf7 29. Rf3+ Ke6 30. Rxf8 Rxf8 31. Qg6+ Kd5 32. Rd1+ Kc4 33. Qe4+ Kb5 34. a4+ Ka5 35. b4+ Kxa4 36. Ra1+ Kb5 37. c4+ Kxb4 38. c5+ Kxc5 39. Rc1+ Kb5 40. Qc4+ Ka5 41. Ra1# {Source: Hereford Times, 1 April 1911} 1-0

